INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "case_study" VALUES(7,1,'Threat Intelligence Programme for a Telecoms Provider','Telecommunications','Mascom Wireless','Mascom Wireless, one of Botswana''s largest mobile network operators, was experiencing a rising volume of SIM swap fraud and SS7 protocol attacks that were being used to intercept customer one-time passwords and drain bank accounts.','CyberNova deployed its AI Cyber Assistant across Mascom''s core network infrastructure, establishing real-time behavioural baselines for all subscriber activity. The AI flagged anomalous SIM swap request patterns within milliseconds, automatically triggering account freezes and alerting the fraud response team. Within 90 days, SIM swap fraud incidents dropped by 94%, saving the organisation an estimated BWP 4.2 million in prevented losses.','2026-05-10 15:34:20');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "case_study" VALUES(9,1,'Securing Patient Data Across a Regional Hospital Network','Bokamoso Private Hospital','Healthcare','Bokamoso Private Hospital in Gaborone identified alarming gaps in the security of its electronic patient records system following an internal audit, with patient data accessible to unauthorised staff and third-party medical suppliers.','CyberNova implemented an AI-driven access anomaly detection layer across Bokamoso''s patient records infrastructure. The system learned normal access patterns for each staff role and flagged deviations in real time. Over 200 unauthorised access events were surfaced in the first month. Role-based access controls were restructured and full POPIA compliance was achieved within 90 days of deployment.','2026-05-10 15:36:15');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "case_study" VALUES(10,1,'Cybersecurity Compliance Overhaul for a Pan-African Insurer','Old Mutual Southern Africa','Insurance','Old Mutual''s Southern Africa division faced mounting pressure from regulators across Botswana, Namibia, and Zimbabwe to demonstrate compliance with evolving data protection legislation including POPIA and local financial sector frameworks.','CyberNova''s AI governance engine mapped Old Mutual''s data processing activities across all three jurisdictions simultaneously, cross-referencing them against POPIA, GDPR equivalents, and local financial regulations. The system surfaced 47 compliance gaps and auto-generated remediation plans for each. A compliance dashboard was delivered giving the legal and risk teams live visibility into their posture across all territories.','2026-05-10 15:37:09');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "case_study" VALUES(11,1,'Ransomware Recovery and Resilience for a Mining Conglomerate','Debswana Diamond Company','Mining','Debswana suffered a ransomware attack that encrypted critical operational data across three mine sites, halting production scheduling and payroll systems for 72 hours and threatening millions in losses.','CyberNova''s incident response team activated within two hours of the breach notification. The AI Cyber Assistant isolated affected network segments, identified the ransomware strain as a LockBit variant, and initiated automated rollback from clean backups. A hardened network architecture was deployed post-recovery, with AI-monitored segmentation across all mine sites to prevent lateral movement in any future attack.','2026-05-10 15:38:44');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "case_study" VALUES(12,1,'Network Hardening Ahead of National Elections','Botswana Electoral Commission','Government','Ahead of the 2024 national elections, the Botswana Electoral Commission sought to protect its voter registration systems and results transmission network from foreign interference and insider threats.','CyberNova conducted a full AI-powered vulnerability assessment of the Commission''s digital infrastructure eight weeks before election day. Critical weaknesses in the results transmission system were identified and patched. The AI Cyber Assistant was deployed to monitor all network activity during the registration and voting periods, generating hourly threat intelligence briefings for the Commission''s IT leadership throughout the election cycle.','2026-05-10 15:41:30');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "case_study" VALUES(13,1,'Securing Online Banking Infrastructure for a Major Retail Bank','First National Bank Botswana','Finance','FNB Botswana experienced a surge in phishing attacks targeting internet banking customers, resulting in unauthorised account access and reputational damage. The bank needed an urgent security overhaul of its digital banking platform.','CyberNova integrated its AI Cyber Assistant into FNB Botswana''s internet banking environment, deploying real-time session anomaly detection to identify suspicious login behaviour and transaction patterns. A customer-facing AI alert system was also configured to notify users of unusual activity instantly. Phishing-related account compromises fell by 81% within the first quarter, and the bank achieved ISO 27001 certification six months after deployment.','2026-05-10 15:42:08');
